name: Bounded chunk inventory discloses partial source work and explicit recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_chunk_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run full-mode:hunt {"dryRun":true,"reuseCachedChunks":false}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_chunk_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | partial-plan
expect: Planning only
expect: partial; execution blocked
resize: 160x48
live-snap: partial-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: partial-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: partial-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: partial-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: partial-40x12
expect: oversized.c
keys: NPage
live-snap: partial-reading-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: partial-reading-40x12-2
keys: NPage
live-snap: partial-reading-40x12-3
ask: Can you identify the omitted source, fixed limits and partial planning outcome across six sizes, without confusing this with a scan or spending approval?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: logs
submit: run full-mode:hunt {"dryRun":true,"scopeFile":"scope.txt","reuseCachedChunks":false}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_chunk_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scoped
paste-file: @ART/explicit-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 selected sources planned | explicit-plan
expect: explicit-scope
ask: Is explicit recovery understandable as a new local plan for the selected vendor source, with no scan job or model request?
keys: Escape
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 0 findings | auxiliary-report
expect-not: Displayed Scan: completed
expect-not: scanned
keys: Home
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | export-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_chunk_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/partial-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | recovered-partial
expect: partial; execution blocked
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_chunk_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the partial receipt and separate explicit plan, without starting a scan or presenting a completed repository scan?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
